1
00:00:01,292 --> 00:00:03,000
Hallo. This is Liam, in for Bear.

2
00:00:03,042 --> 00:00:04,958
Better teaching pictures do more than
decorate.

3
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:09,042
These twenty-four isometric props make
actions visible: selecting

4
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:12,125
evidence, granting permission, handing off
work, and recording

5
00:00:12,125 --> 00:00:12,625
decisions.

6
00:00:13,542 --> 00:00:15,792
Three terms. A prop is a reusable drawing.

7
00:00:16,042 --> 00:00:18,083
A state tells us what condition it is in.

8
00:00:18,292 --> 00:00:20,125
An action changes that condition.

9
00:00:20,542 --> 00:00:23,042
The picture shows the change; the voice
explains why

10
00:00:23,042 --> 00:00:23,458
it matters.

11
00:00:24,333 --> 00:00:25,667
Start with a dataset.

12
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:27,208
Lift one record out of the collection.

13
00:00:27,708 --> 00:00:30,792
The motion distinguishes the evidence we
actually inspect from

14
00:00:30,792 --> 00:00:32,000
everything we could inspect.

15
00:00:33,042 --> 00:00:34,500
Linked data adds a relationship.

16
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,292
Join the connector to the records.

17
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:39,333
A link tells us where material connects,
not whether

18
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:40,625
that material is reliable.

19
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:44,625
Layers separate responsibilities. Lift the
top layer while the

20
00:00:44,625 --> 00:00:47,458
others stay put. Use this to distinguish
the interface,

21
00:00:47,708 --> 00:00:49,542
the agent, and the underlying service.

22
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:52,458
A reference gives the worker a procedure
when it

23
00:00:52,458 --> 00:00:54,417
is needed. Pull out the marked section.

24
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:58,208
Keep instructions visually distinct from
evidence about the world.

25
00:00:58,875 --> 00:01:01,417
The terminal takes a request and returns a
result.

26
00:01:01,792 --> 00:01:04,083
Watch the evidence slip enter, then a
different slip

27
00:01:04,083 --> 00:01:07,042
emerge. An action has an observable
consequence.

28
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:10,583
Connected services exchange something
specific.

29
00:01:10,917 --> 00:01:13,292
Draw the connection, then send a packet
across it.

30
00:01:13,542 --> 00:01:16,083
Do not use a cable to imply unlimited
access.

31
00:01:16,958 --> 00:01:19,625
Deployment moves a package into its
operating position.

32
00:01:19,958 --> 00:01:21,750
Lower the code onto its platform.

33
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:25,125
This shows delivery, not a guarantee that
the software

34
00:01:25,125 --> 00:01:25,958
works correctly.

35
00:01:26,708 --> 00:01:28,375
A network offers more than one route.

36
00:01:28,667 --> 00:01:30,208
Follow one packet through the nodes.

37
00:01:30,708 --> 00:01:33,042
Showing the chosen path is clearer than
lighting up

38
00:01:33,042 --> 00:01:34,250
every connection at once.

39
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:37,042
The raised hand means stop and ask.

40
00:01:37,292 --> 00:01:39,083
Raise it before the action continues.

41
00:01:39,542 --> 00:01:42,542
Human intervention belongs inside the
workflow, not in a

42
00:01:42,542 --> 00:01:43,583
disclaimer after it.

43
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:47,333
A reviewer inspects a proposed result
before approving it.

44
00:01:47,625 --> 00:01:49,583
Bring the evidence to the person, then add
the

45
00:01:49,583 --> 00:01:52,167
check. Approval is a decision, not
decoration.

46
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:54,625
Agreement needs two sides.

47
00:01:54,875 --> 00:01:57,125
Bring the hands together only after both
are present.

48
00:01:57,667 --> 00:02:00,083
Use this for accepted terms or a shared
task

49
00:02:00,083 --> 00:02:01,875
boundary, not automatic trust.

50
00:02:02,667 --> 00:02:04,500
A handoff transfers responsibility.

51
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,417
Move the same evidence slip from one
person to

52
00:02:07,417 --> 00:02:10,375
another. The object persists, so the
viewer can follow

53
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:11,542
what changed hands.

54
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:14,875
A policy is a constraint that changes
behavior.

55
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,500
Let a request approach the boundary and
stop.

56
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:20,000
If the rule never affects the action, the
picture

57
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:20,792
teaches nothing.

58
00:02:21,583 --> 00:02:22,542
Permission is a gate.

59
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:25,292
Keep the lock closed until access is
granted, then

60
00:02:25,292 --> 00:02:28,583
open it. The shield represents this
boundary, not proof

61
00:02:28,583 --> 00:02:29,708
that a system is secure.

62
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,000
Uncertainty should change the route.

63
00:02:32,375 --> 00:02:34,583
Send the unresolved case away for review.

64
00:02:35,042 --> 00:02:37,417
A question mark is useful only when the
workflow

65
00:02:37,417 --> 00:02:38,500
does something about it.

66
00:02:39,208 --> 00:02:41,042
A key grants a particular capability.

67
00:02:41,458 --> 00:02:42,708
Move it to the access point.

68
00:02:43,042 --> 00:02:45,125
In your own lesson, name what it unlocks
and

69
00:02:45,125 --> 00:02:46,667
what remains outside its scope.

70
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:50,208
Cross-check two records before adding
either check mark.

71
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:52,667
These symbols show the comparison step.

72
00:02:52,875 --> 00:02:55,375
They cannot tell us whether the underlying
sources are

73
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:56,583
independent or correct.

74
00:02:57,375 --> 00:02:58,917
Inspection is an active search.

75
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:01,542
Move the lens across the source, then mark
the

76
00:03:01,542 --> 00:03:05,208
selected finding. Finding a passage and
verifying its claim

77
00:03:05,208 --> 00:03:05,958
are different jobs.

78
00:03:06,792 --> 00:03:08,708
Revision needs a before and an after.

79
00:03:09,125 --> 00:03:11,500
Separate the versions and reveal the
changed line.

80
00:03:11,917 --> 00:03:14,292
Keep enough history to explain why the new
version

81
00:03:14,292 --> 00:03:14,792
is better.

82
00:03:15,583 --> 00:03:17,750
A process record accumulates as work
happens.

83
00:03:18,042 --> 00:03:19,250
Add each row in order.

84
00:03:19,708 --> 00:03:22,292
Record the action, the evidence, and the
decision, not

85
00:03:22,292 --> 00:03:23,417
just the finished artifact.

86
00:03:24,375 --> 00:03:26,542
Delegation starts with a responsible
owner.

87
00:03:26,875 --> 00:03:29,500
Draw the branches, then send work to each
destination.

88
00:03:30,083 --> 00:03:33,458
Different workers need explicit tasks, not
merely different boxes.

89
00:03:34,292 --> 00:03:35,833
A decision changes the path.

90
00:03:36,167 --> 00:03:38,417
Split the moving token into two possible
routes.

91
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:41,333
In a real workflow, state the condition
that selects

92
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:42,542
one route rather than both.

93
00:03:43,375 --> 00:03:45,083
Rebase is a code-history metaphor.

94
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:46,875
Move the branch to a later base.

95
00:03:47,375 --> 00:03:50,208
This is a simplified illustration of
changing its starting

96
00:03:50,208 --> 00:03:52,208
point, not a complete Git tutorial.

97
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,625
A conveyor makes progress visible.

98
00:03:55,042 --> 00:03:57,125
Move the package along the belt, then stop
it

99
00:03:57,125 --> 00:03:59,792
for review. Finishing the motion is not
the same

100
00:03:59,792 --> 00:04:00,708
as passing the check.

101
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:04,792
These props are simplified redraws adapted
from Isocons under

102
00:04:04,792 --> 00:04:07,792
Creative Commons Attribution four point
zero.

103
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:10,417
The shapes, colors, and animation have
changed.

104
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:12,917
Keep the source and license credit when
you reuse

105
00:04:12,917 --> 00:04:13,208
them.

106
00:04:13,875 --> 00:04:16,375
Your turn. Paste this into Claude: Use
Show-Tell to

107
00:04:16,375 --> 00:04:18,375
explain my workflow with three props.

108
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:20,792
Show one human decision and one check of
the

109
00:04:20,792 --> 00:04:22,750
evidence. Then check the film yourself.

110
00:04:23,167 --> 00:04:24,833
Does every motion explain a change?

111
00:04:25,083 --> 00:04:26,542
Can you tell what the human decided?

112
00:04:27,875 --> 00:04:29,458
Show-Tell: 24 Props That Explain.

113
00:04:29,458 --> 00:04:30,708
At Nik Bear Brown.
